#
# onyx_debug_reduction.fragment - trim debug/diagnostic features
#
# Tree: seventeen @ 6.6.142. The cost figures below were MEASURED on this
# tree, not carried over from the 6.6.82 one. Method: build the merged
# defconfig three ways (no reduction / this list / this list plus
# -d CONFIG_PROFILING), run olddefconfig on each, and diff the resulting
# .config files. Both make and olddefconfig exit 0 in every case, which is
# the whole problem: nothing here fails the build.
#
# Every symbol here is chosen because turning it off does not resize or
# reorder any exported struct, so the GKI ABI is untouched. That is what makes
# this safe to apply on a kernel whose vendor modules are built against the
# frozen GKI symbol list.
#
# MEASURED COST of this list: exactly 6 symbols are lost.
#   CC_HAS_UBSAN_ARRAY_BOUNDS  (hidden symbol derived from the compiler check)
#   UBSAN_ARRAY_BOUNDS  UBSAN_BOUNDS  UBSAN_LOCAL_BOUNDS
#   UBSAN_SANITIZE_ALL  UBSAN_TRAP
# Nothing else. CONFIG_PROFILING, PERF_EVENTS, BPF_LSM, ARM_PMU and UPROBES
# all survive, which is the point.
#
# (diffconfig also prints 8 "-UBSAN_* n" lines; those are symbols that were
# already unset and are merely no longer printed once the parent is gone.
# build-onyx.yml's gate 3 filters exactly that form.)
#
# Deliberately NOT in this list:
#
#   CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO_BTF      must stay on; it is what eBPF/CO-RE needs.
#   CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO_REDUCED  must stay OFF. It is a hard blocker for BTF
#                              (lib/Kconfig.debug:376: DEBUG_INFO_BTF depends
#                              on !DEBUG_INFO_SPLIT && !DEBUG_INFO_REDUCED)
#                              and dropping it silently is exactly the kind of
#                              failure gate 3 exists to catch.
#

# Slabs / boot-time debug knobs
# CONFIG_DEBUG_MISC is not set
# CONFIG_DEBUG_MEMORY_INIT is not set
# CONFIG_CMA_DEBUGFS is not set
# CONFIG_CLEANCACHE is not set

# Printk verbosity
# CONFIG_PRINTK_CALLER is not set
# CONFIG_PRINTK_TIME is not set

# RCU stall tracing
# CONFIG_RCU_TRACE is not set

# Bluetooth debugfs
# CONFIG_BT_DEBUGFS is not set

# UBSan. The sub-options are listed explicitly as well: the parent being
# unset is not something kconfig propagates to every child.
# CONFIG_UBSAN is not set
# CONFIG_UBSAN_BOUNDS is not set
# CONFIG_UBSAN_ARRAY_BOUNDS is not set
# CONFIG_UBSAN_LOCAL_BOUNDS is not set
# CONFIG_UBSAN_SANITIZE_ALL is not set
# CONFIG_UBSAN_TRAP is not set


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DO NOT ADD CONFIG_PROFILING HERE.
#
# gki-clo's reduction list did include it. Measured on THIS tree (6.6.142),
# adding `-d CONFIG_PROFILING` costs 10 further symbols on top of the 6 above:
#
#   ARM_PMU  ARM_PMUV3  HAVE_HW_BREAKPOINT  HW_PERF_EVENTS
#   BPF_EVENTS  BPF_LSM  UPROBES  UPROBE_EVENTS
#   GUEST_PERF_EVENTS  UID_SYS_STATS
#
# i.e. every hardware performance counter, all uprobe support, and BPF LSM
# disappear from a kernel that still builds cleanly with exit 0. That directly
# defeats the point of shipping BTF for eBPF: CONFIG_BPF_LSM is what
# CO-RE/BPF LSM programs attach to.
#
# The 6.6.82 tree measured 27 symbols for the same experiment. The count moved
# with the kernel; the conclusion did not. Re-measure if this list is ever
# changed, using the method in the header.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
